{"name":"Woollen Sox","hex":"#dcc9ad","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woollen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of woolen."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of woolen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woollen"},{"term":"sox","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Swo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of sock (footwear)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woolen","blocks":[{"text":"Woolen or woollen is a type of yarn made from carded wool. Woolen yarn is soft, light, stretchy, and full of air. It is thus a good insulator, and makes a good knitting yarn. Woolen yarn is in contrast to worsted yarn, in which the fibers are combed to lie parallel rather than carded, producing a hard, strong yarn."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woolen","wikidata":"Q1751888"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"sox":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Yangolin-sox.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Yangolin-sox.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Yangolin-sox.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Yangolin-sox.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Yangolin-sox.wav.ogg"}]}}}